<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Nimoy returns for his six-month COPD review. He has kept up the home exercise program, walking about 15 minutes twice a day and doing his strength routine three times a week. He still walks about 300 meters before stopping and uses a wheelchair for long distances such as airports. He uses albuterol about twice a week and takes every maintenance dose. He has had no flare-up, antibiotic or prednisone course, emergency visit, or hospital stay since he started treatment. The summer heat made him more breathless on a few afternoons, and he walked in the early morning instead. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exercise</td><td>Home program kept up; walks about 300 meters before stopping</td></tr><tr><td>Reliever use</td><td>Albuterol about twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>All maintenance doses taken</td></tr><tr><td>Exacerbations</td><td>None in six months of treatment, and none in the past 12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Triggers</td><td>Hot afternoons; walks early in the day</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

