    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">COPD, GOLD 3, group B, stable (J44.9)</content>. CAT 14 and mMRC grade 2, with no exacerbation in six months; resting saturation 94 percent. The gains from rehabilitation have held. No change in treatment is needed. [S]<list><item>Continue tiotropium-olodaterol and albuterol as needed.</item><item>Continue the home exercise program, walking in the cooler part of the day.</item><item>High-dose influenza and RSV vaccines at the annual wellness visit in October.</item><item>Yearly spirometry at the February review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>COPD Assessment Test (CAT)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>14, stable</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>mMRC dyspnea grade</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Grade 2, stable</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Exacerbation history and GOLD group</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None in the past 12 months; group B</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pulse oximetry</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>94 percent at rest on room air</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Smoking status and cessation support</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>BMI and nutritional status</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>BMI 23.7; weight stable</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Inhaler technique and adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Correct; full adherence</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Long-term oxygen assessment</td><td>As indicated: resting saturation 88 percent or less, confirmed twice at least three weeks apart</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Resting saturation 94 percent</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Pulmonary rehabilitation</td><td>Eligibility reviewed yearly and after any hospital stay</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Completed in May; home program kept up</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Spirometry</td><td>At diagnosis, then at least yearly and with significant clinical change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Due at the yearly review in February</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mood and comorbidity screening</td><td>At diagnosis and yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>Due at the annual wellness visit in October</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Vaccination status</td><td>Reviewed yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza and RSV vaccines planned for the annual wellness visit before the respiratory virus season; COVID-19 vaccine this autumn</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>CAT score at least 2 points lower by the three-month review. Outcome by 2026-05-12: CAT fell from 22 to 15 [S]</item><item>6-minute walk distance at least 30 meters farther after pulmonary rehabilitation. Outcome by 2026-05-12: 270 m at entry and 330 m at exit [S]</item><item>No moderate or severe exacerbation over the six months after starting maintenance therapy. Outcome by 2026-08-11: No exacerbation, oral corticosteroid course, antibiotic course, or emergency visit in six months [S]</item><item>Correct soft mist inhaler technique and a daily maintenance dose. Outcome by 2026-03-10: Correct technique on demonstration and no missed doses by dose counter at four weeks [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for the Diagnosis, Management, and Prevention of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, 2025 report (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease monograph (2026); Pulmonary Rehabilitation for Adults with Chronic Respiratory Disease: An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2023); Home Oxygen Therapy for Adults with Chronic Lung Disease: An Official American Thoracic Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2020); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit in October. COPD review in about six months with spirometry, or the same day for any flare-up. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
